    "type": "ED note",
    "author": "H. Castillo, MD (Emergency Medicine)",
    "author_role": "provider",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-25T12:50",
    "text": "CC: Vomiting, diarrhea, lightheaded.\n\nHPI: 74F with HTN, T2DM and HLD with 3 days of nonbloody watery diarrhea (6-8/day) and vomiting, unable to keep fluids down x24 h. Husband had the same illness last week, now recovered. Lightheaded on standing. No abd pain, fever, or recent antibiotics.\n\nVitals: T 37.4, HR 104, BP 102/58 (orthostatic drop to 84/50 standing), RR 18, SpO2 98% RA.\nExam: Dry mucous membranes, poor skin turgor. Abd soft, hyperactive BS, nontender.\n\nLabs: Na 128, K 3.7, Cl 94, HCO3 20, BUN 52, Cr 2.3 (baseline 0.8, 04/2026), Glu 162. WBC 9.1. Lipase normal. UA: SG 1.030, no infection.\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n1. AKI, likely prerenal from dehydration due to gastroenteritis. 2 L NS bolus, ondansetron.\n2. Hyponatremia.\nDispo: Admit to medicine."
   },
   {
    "id": "d2",
    "type": "H&P",
    "author": "R. Iqbal, MD (Hospital Medicine)",
    "author_role": "provider",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-25T17:20",
    "text": "HISTORY AND PHYSICAL\n\nHPI: See ED. Tolerating sips after ondansetron.\n\nPMH: HTN. T2DM (A1c 6.9%, no complications). HLD.\nMeds: lisinopril/HCTZ 20/12.5 mg daily, metformin 500 mg BID, simvastatin 20 mg qHS.\n\nExam: HR 96, BP 112/64, mucosa dry. Abd benign.\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n1. Acute kidney injury - prerenal, due to dehydration from viral gastroenteritis. Cr 2.3 from baseline 0.8. NS at 125 mL/h, hold lisinopril/HCTZ and metformin, strict I/O, BMP q12h.\n2. Dehydration - IV fluids as above.\n3. Hyponatremia, hypovolemic - Na 128 from GI losses; isotonic fluids, goal correction <8 mEq/L per 24 h.\n4. Viral gastroenteritis - likely norovirus given sick contact; supportive care, ondansetron PRN, advance diet. Stool studies not indicated.\n5. T2DM - hold metformin; correction scale insulin.\n6. HTN - hold antihypertensives while hypovolemic.\n7. HLD - continue simvastatin."
   },
   {
    "id": "d3",
